-- One-time data update: Portes du Soleil Run gets a new layout.
--
-- Its own layout (Moses, 15 Nov 2026: the World Tour re-layouts): until now
-- nearly the same track as Åre Run and Greenland Expedition. Its classic start
-- down from Avoriaz past the cows kept (the field now let go in waves), then a
-- sweep across the French-Swiss border under the chairlift, down the Swiss Wall
-- from Chavanette (the big feature and signature: the steepest stretch, low
-- moguls down it), the hairpin, S-bends into the Swiss village, the forest
-- spiral and the run to the village square. Its name, slug, look and past races
-- stay. Its track record, country records and players' personal bests start
-- again from now (tracks.records_since); past results stay. Races already run
-- keep their stored replays and play back exactly as they ran.
--
-- Generated from src/game/physicsTracks.js by scripts/physics-track-sql.js --relayout.
-- Only the Portes du Soleil Run track row changes.

